From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:14:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Stop the started subdevs when stream
 start fails

video_start_streaming() enables the subdevs from the video node
towards the sensor. When one of them fails, the error path only stops
the media pipeline, so the subdevs already enabled stay streaming. The
next start then hits the s_stream() state check in call_s_stream() for
each of them (one WARNING per subdev), leaves the hardware as it was,
and the capture hangs in VIDIOC_DQBUF with "VFE sof timeout", "VFE reg
update timeout" and "VFE halt timeout" errors. Only reloading the
driver recovers.

Disable the subdevs enabled before the failing one, in the same order
video_stop_streaming() uses.

Tested on a Galaxy Tab S3 (APQ8096) with imx258 start failures forced
(CCI kept runtime active across sensor power cycles, see the CCI
timeout fix): the stream after each failure starts and captures
normally. The failed start itself now also logs "VFE sof timeout" and
"VFE reg update timeout" while the VFE that never got a frame is
stopped.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c    | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
index 0852eb6f13..c0f9f4d00e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-video.c
@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ static int video_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int count)
 {
 	struct camss_video *video = vb2_get_drv_priv(q);
 	struct video_device *vdev = &video->vdev;
-	struct media_entity *entity;
+	struct media_entity *entity, *failed;
 	struct media_pad *pad;
 	struct v4l2_subdev *subdev;
 	int ret;
@@ -283,11 +283,25 @@ static int video_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int count)
 
 		ret = v4l2_subdev_call(subdev, video, s_stream, 1);
 		if (ret < 0 && ret != -ENOIOCTLCMD)
-			goto error;
+			goto error_stream;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
 
+error_stream:
+	/* Stop the subdevs started before the one that failed */
+	failed = entity;
+	entity = &vdev->entity;
+	while (1) {
+		pad = media_pad_remote_pad_first(&entity->pads[0]);
+		entity = pad->entity;
+		if (entity == failed)
+			break;
+
+		subdev = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(entity);
+		v4l2_subdev_call(subdev, video, s_stream, 0);
+	}
+
 error:
 	video_device_pipeline_stop(vdev);
 
